            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical course of hepato-gastro-duodenal diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To characterize clinical course of hepatogastroduodenal diseases (HGDD).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">897 patients with HGDD were examined aged 15 to 82 years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Three groups of patients were recognized: with predominant symptoms of pains in epigastric and hepatic area; with motor-evacuatory disturbances of the stomach and duodenum; with prevailing symptoms of asthenovegetative and depressive disorders.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Distribution of the patients by type of clinical course provides algorithm of examination and helps to formulate optimal therapeutic policy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
